lines += ['', f"**Predefined coarse null-calibration screen: {'PASS' if a['null_screen_passed'] else 'FAIL'}.** At the much rarer intended temporal-gate threshold 0.001/12, {a['rare_tail_count']}/{a['null_n']} clean references were flagged. This count is descriptive; 9000 trials cannot establish precise calibration at that rare tail. The unadjusted 5% check at correlation 0.95 showed 125 versus 150 expected flags, consistent with some conservatism; it did not fail the predefined multiplicity-adjusted screen.", '', f"A separate variance-mismatch check increased only temporal noise amplitude to 1.25 at correlation 0.95. The test detected {a['defects_detected']}/{a['defect_n']} cases, passing the predefined 90% power screen. This tests one defect size, not arbitrary background changes.", '', f"On the saved MG178 primary references, the old method rejected {len(oldbad)}/{len(clean)} valid backgrounds. None of those {len(oldbad)} is flagged by the new temporal diagnostic, and the new temporal diagnostic flags {sum(r['profile_temporal_tail'] for r in clean)}/{len(clean)} in total. This is a diagnostic application to development data, not a new accepted-path denominator or a rescore of MG178.", '', 'The new variance-consistency test does not replace species, coherent-mean or spectral checks. The shape-X and contaminated-reference cases can have consistent spatial and temporal scalar variance while violating other assumptions. A valid reference also cannot certify that tracking-time conditions will remain unchanged. Joint profiling here does not yet propagate correlation uncertainty through tracker likelihoods, geometry selection or predictive fit guards.','', '## Displaced-Y false single','', 'The target is MG178 early regime 0.1, independent-time noise amplitude 1.25, displaced-Y replicate 1, observation 15. Y had been shifted by 16 sites beginning at observation 10.','', '| Frozen target quantity | Value |','|---|---:|',f"| Single-core model weight | {r['class_weights']['single']:.6g} |",f"| X-only model weight | {r['class_weights']['Xonly']:.6g} |",f"| Innovation quadratic / limit | {r['innovation_q']:.6g} / {r['qcut']:.6g} |",f"| Selected / true primary center | {r['selected_center']} / {r['truth_center']} |",f"| Selected width | {r['selected_width']:.6g} |",f"| Center spread / allowed | {r['center_spread']} / 4 |",f"| Width spread / allowed | {r['width_spread']:.6g} / 0.25 |", '', 'The primary location was correct, both spread guards passed, and the global noise-fit quadratic was below its limit. However, the alternatives were absent, intact aligned single, X-only, Y-only and two separated full XY cores. None explicitly describes a surviving X feature with a displaced Y feature. X-only omits Y rather than representing its shifted location; the two-core model adds an entire second XY structure and requires wider separation. A high normalized weight among these alternatives therefore does not establish that X and Y remain aligned.','', 'The conditional audit supplied the true primary center and width and compared aligned X/Y with 48 possible nonzero relative Y shifts from -24 to +24 sites. The shift alternative integrated all 48 possibilities uniformly; it was not told the actual shift of 16. Known-shift results below are separate oracle diagnostics. All fields and labels were saved MG178 data.','', '| Target conditional diagnostic | Value |','|---|---:|',f"| Known shift 16 log likelihood ratio versus aligned | {r['oracle_shift16_logBF']:.6g} |",f"| Full uniform 48-shift log likelihood ratio | {r['uniform_shift_logBF']:.6g} |",f"| Squared noise-weighted difference, shift 16 versus aligned | {r['oracle_squared_separation']:.6g} |",f"| Redrawn shift filter: displaced weight | {r['redrawn_displaced_weight']:.6g} |",f"| Persistent shift filter: displaced weight | {r['persistent_displaced_weight']:.6g} |", '', 'Both conditional filters strongly favor misalignment at the failed deadline. Across all 12 displaced-Y paths in this audit, the persistent-shift diagnostic exceeded 0.999994 at observation 15. None of the 12 matched moving aligned controls reached 0.95 displaced weight anywhere; the largest weight was 0.111108. These results show useful information under supplied primary geometry, not performance of a deployable alignment classifier. The audit covers only independent-time noise and a finite displacement family.','', 'The global residual safeguard measures fit across 998 noise dimensions. A localized, scientifically important species mismatch need not exceed its overall tolerance. That is why explicit component alternatives or a separately validated local component safeguard are needed; simply tightening the global threshold could reject many intact noisy cores.','', '## Verification and retention','', f"Separate checking passed {c['independent_profile_fits']} independently bracketed profile fits, {c['fit_pvalues']} fitted p-values and all calibration-tail decisions, {c['selected_generator_covariance_checks']} selected Gaussian-generator/dense covariance checks, {c['full_shift_grids']} full 48-shift grids, {c['temporal_filter_steps']} probability-domain filter steps and {c['unchanged_labels']} frozen labels. Maximum profile LR difference was {c['max_LR_difference']:.6g}. Main analysis also passed {a['realspace_shift_checks']} real-space shift checks; maximum difference {a['max_shift_difference']:.6g}. These share input/template models and the same author, and are not external replication.", '', f"Analysis took {a['elapsed_seconds']:.6g} seconds; separate checking {c['elapsed_seconds']:.6g} seconds. Gaussian calibration sufficient statistics and fit results are losslessly compressed in `calibration_statistics.json.gz`; the sufficient statistics preserve the full information used by this Gaussian likelihood. Full coordinate draws were transient and were not retained, as specified; deterministic seeds permit regeneration. All actual MG178 full field inputs remain local in `local_raw/MG178_persistent`. No bulk fields were uploaded.", '', '## Recommended next step','', 'Specify a new complete instrument with an explicit displaced/partially aligned species alternative, including persistent component offsets and shared-primary geometry uncertainty. Integrate the profile-based background correction and define how estimation uncertainty enters predictive and structural tests. Then use fresh aligned, displaced, missing, split and weak-core controls, including motion during acquisition and correlated noise. Do not count this known-primary audit as qualification or choose an alignment threshold from its failed path.','', 'The background profile prototype passed its limited statistical screens. The complete tracker remains unqualified, MG178 remains FAILED, earlier MG176/MG163 results are unchanged, and G remains unresolved. No new kinetic production is authorized by this result. PI closure is pending.', '', '![Statistical calibration and conditional alignment diagnostic](MG179_diagnostics.png)']
